From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:16:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] diagnostic: bound Madai MX startup to the observed
 ceiling

The CPR-disabled 6.18.64 RAM control boots with acknowledged active and sleep votes at 1287500 uV, while the preceding 1337500 uV control resets before an acknowledgement is retained. Keep the live APC guard and voltage-plan rejection paths. Use the complete validated plan ceiling for the CPR sleep guard and runtime request ceiling. This is a per-unit diagnostic pending CPR hardware qualification, not a universal PM8226 limit or an installed update.

(cherry picked from commit 4cb942677a07683bc8c7341829a96ad004704630)
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts | 4 ++--
 drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr.c                          | 5 +++--
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts
index 92340f2bf..e91112c55 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts
@@ -229,12 +229,12 @@ regulators {
 
 		pm8226_l3_ao: l3-ao {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <750000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1337500>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1287500>;
 		};
 
 		pm8226_l3_so: l3-so {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <750000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1337500>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1287500>;
 		};
 	};
 };
diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr.c b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr.c
index 7b2492139..8d09464d3 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr.c
@@ -1309,13 +1309,14 @@ static int __maybe_unused cpr_msm8926_init(struct cpr_drv *drv)
 			data->calibration.ring_osc[i] : 0;
 		fuse->step_quot = 30;
 	}
-	ret = cpr_sleep_vote_init(drv->dev, 1337500, &data->mx_sleep);
+	ret = cpr_sleep_vote_init(drv->dev, data->plan.bootstrap_mx_uV,
+				  &data->mx_sleep);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(drv->dev, ret, "MX sleep guard unavailable\n");
 
 	drv->cpu_clk = cpu_clk;
 	drv->rails.mx = mx;
-	drv->rails.mx_max_uV = 1337500;
+	drv->rails.mx_max_uV = data->plan.bootstrap_mx_uV;
 	drv->msm8926 = data;
 	return 0;
 }
